ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "2.0.5", text = "|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Move any window: the mouse wheel over a window zooms the camera again; only Ctrl + mouse wheel resizes the window.\n• Chat: Copy Line is gone.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Fake CM: a bar you take off the cooldown display can be clicked again right away, without a reload.\n• Move any window: Ctrl + right-click to reset a window's size no longer pins a window you never moved, and does nothing in combat on windows the game locks.\n• Gray out known items: turning it off clears the grey from the vendor page at once.\n• Chat Formatting: the explanations now match what each option does." },
    { version = "2.0.4", text = "New Quality of Life helpers, your chat formatting back, and a settings panel that explains every option on its own.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n|cffffffffQuality of Life|r (all off until you switch them on)\n• |cffffffffGray out known items:|r recipes and items you already know are greyed out at vendors.\n• |cffffffffMail address book:|r a button beside Send Mail's \"To:\" lists your other characters and the last one you mailed.\n• |cffffffffAlert sounds:|r ready checks, summons, resurrections, group invites and dungeon queues flash the taskbar and play a sound, even with sound effects off.\n• |cffffffffPet food marker:|r a paw marks the food in your bags your hunter pet eats.\n• |cffffffffSkip loot confirmations:|r no \"will bind to you\" question when you loot or roll.\n• |cffffffffCombat enemy plates:|r enemy nameplates show only during fights.\n• |cffffffffFrame numbers:|r hides the damage numbers on your portrait and the health and power numbers on Blizzard's frames.\n\n|cffffffffMore options|r\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffUpdate spell ranks|r: a newly learned rank replaces the old one on your bars (lower ranks you placed on purpose stay).\n• Chat, Damage Meter and Quest Tracker: |cffffffffFrame Border|r, with None to hide it.\n• Move any window: |cffffffffCtrl + mouse wheel|r resizes a window again; Ctrl + right-click resets it.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Chat: the |cffffffffFormatting|r options are back (better NPC and player names, timestamps, short channel names, level before names).\n• Settings panel: every option has its own explanation, with lists where it helps, and the dog is back in the info panel.\n• Chat has Frame, Tweaks and Fonts tabs; Quality of Life has Gameplay, Interface and Advanced tabs; Tooltips has Look and Tweaks sections; Quest Tracker has a Frame section, with Display above Minimize.\n• Action Bars: Fake Cooldown Manager has its own |cffffffffFakeCM|r tab and no on/off switch: it's on while a bar is picked.\n• A few options have clearer names, like |cffffffffTrain all skills|r and |cffffffffHide level box|r.\n• Translations: the dots and bullets that kept some phrases from translating are gone.\n• FlareUI is about 7 MB smaller.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Dungeon Journal's minimap button goes in the addon drawer and can be clicked.\n• Legacy Forever's tracker section no longer disappears when FlareUI's quest tracker is on.\n• Clicking a link in the settings opens the copy box in front of the panel, with a sound." },
    { version = "2.0.3", text = "|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Unit Frames: with |cffffffffHide Player and Pet|r on, your player and pet frames now show at the same moment as the target frame when you pick a target, instead of a moment later." },
    { version = "2.0.2", text = "|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffHide Player and Pet|r (was Hide Player and Pet out of combat) hid your frames too often. They now hide only while you're out of combat, have no target and are at full health. Pointing at either frame still shows both." },
    { version = "2.0.1", text = "You asked for your options back: fonts, textures, fade speeds and more are in. The settings are easier to scan too.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n|cffffffffFonts|r\n• A Fonts tab on Action Bars, Unit Frames, Resource Bars, Buffs & Debuffs, Chat, Damage Meter, Quest Tracker and Tooltips: font, size, outline and shadow for each text.\n\n|cffffffffLook|r\n• |cffffffffBar Texture|r and |cffffffffBorder Texture|r for each unit frame (player, target, focus, pet, their targets, party, raid, boss, cast bar) and each resource bar, in a Look section of its Edit Mode dialog. The Forever style's bronze frames keep their own border.\n\n|cffffffffFading|r\n• |cffffffffFade Speed|r (Instant, Fast, Slow) for action bars, chat and the damage meter.\n• Action bars: five fade groups instead of three.\n• Chat: |cffffffffVisibility|r (Always visible, Chat interactions, Combat + chat interactions) and |cffffffffFade Delay|r (how long the chat stays after showing).\n• Damage meter: every show and hide fades, whether combat, a group or the mouse brings it.\n\n|cffffffffMore options|r\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffHide Player and Pet out of combat|r. Pointing at either one shows both.\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffXP Bar Text|r, on mouseover or always.\n• Chat: |cffffffffEdit Box Opacity|r.\n• Damage Meter: switches for the |cffffffffCombat timer|r, the |cffffffffReady check button|r and the |cffffffffCountdown button|r.\n• Quest Tracker: a |cffffffffDisplay|r section (zone headings, completed last, quest tags, wrap long text, tracked recipes, quest count, hide when empty) and |cffffffffMinimize to a button|r.\n• Tooltips: |cffffffffTooltip Scale|r, |cffffffffHealth bar|r and |cffffffffShow target|r.\n• Minimap: |cffffffffFPS and Latency on Clock|r can be turned off.\n\n|cffffffffSettings panel|r\n• Click a section's title to fold it away.\n• Shorter, clearer explanations in the info panel, with lists where it helps.\n• Two columns for switches, and a taller window.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• The player frame's Show option moved from Edit Mode to the Unit Frames page (Hide Player and Pet out of combat).\n• Chat: the tab menu's Font Size is gone. Set the chat's size in Settings > Chat > Fonts.\n• Damage meter: with Threat view in combat, the meter switches back to damage only once it has faded out after a fight.\n• Action bars fade out a moment sooner after the mouse leaves.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• The sound of picking a target is back.\n• The flight path window can be moved again. The clock, opened mail, the stable, loot history, the group finder lists and the dressing room can be moved too.\n• Unit frame and party, raid and boss borders sit flush against the bars, with no gap.\n• Your 1.x settings brought over by the import now include fonts, textures, the new options and the tooltip scale." },
